  "text": "# Support ticket export: escalation thread\n\n**Queue:** Tier 2 Cities / Nashik\n**Export generated:** 29 April 2024, 18:42 IST\n**Exported by:** joseph.mathai@sahajfresh.in\n**Filter:** severity >= 2, disposition open or escalated, hub = NSK-1, window 12 Apr to 29 Apr\n\n---\n\n## Ticket SF-NSK-118204\n\n**Opened:** 19 Apr 2024, 07:14\n**Subscriber:** 9822-xxx-441, Gangapur Road, Nashik\n**Product:** Curd 400g x 2 (Category A)\n**Disposition:** DISP-07 / product condition, returned at door\n**Agent:** rukhsana.p\n\n> **07:14 rukhsana.p (call notes):** Customer says curd pouches were \"loose\", she pressed one and it was watery, refused both. Rider Sandeep confirmed he took them back. Customer polite but says this is second time this month, first time she did not complain.\n>\n> **07:22 rukhsana.p:** Refund of Rs 96 processed to wallet. Offered a replacement on tomorrow's run, she declined.\n>\n> **07:24 rukhsana.p (internal):** Trip TR-NSK-0419-03. Rider says the box \"felt warm\" when he opened it at the third stop but the van reading was fine when he left the hub at 04:50.\n\n---\n\n## Ticket SF-NSK-118331\n\n**Opened:** 23 Apr 2024, 06:58\n**Subscriber:** 9730-xxx-018, Prabhat Sankul, Sharanpur Road, Nashik\n**Product:** Curd 400g x 1, Buttermilk 1L x 1\n**Disposition:** DISP-07 / product condition, returned at door\n**Agent:** rukhsana.p\n\n> **06:58 rukhsana.p (chat transcript, verbatim):**\n> *Customer:* the curd is sour today, again. we have been with you 14 months\n> *Agent:* I am very sorry sir. May I arrange a refund and a replacement?\n> *Customer:* refund is fine. but you should check what is happening, three houses in our building said the same yesterday\n> *Agent:* I will note that sir and pass it to the hub team.\n>\n> **07:05 rukhsana.p (internal):** He says three neighbours reported the same on 22 Apr. I checked, only one of those is in the system (SF-NSK-118298, closed as DISP-09 no fault found because customer accepted a replacement). Should I reopen 118298?\n\n---\n\n## Ticket SF-NSK-118402\n\n**Opened:** 26 Apr 2024, 07:31\n**Subscriber:** 9421-xxx-772, Indira Nagar, Nashik\n**Product:** Curd 400g x 3\n**Disposition:** DISP-07 / product condition, escalated\n**Agent:** rukhsana.p\n\n> **07:31 rukhsana.p:** Same complaint pattern. All three pouches. Rider took them back. Refund Rs 144.\n>\n> **09:10 rukhsana.p (internal, escalating to team lead):** Joseph, this is the third one on curd out of NSK-1 in eight days and all of them are on the early routes. Bengaluru queue has nothing like this in the same period, I checked. Do I raise it to the hub or is this a known thing?\n\n---\n\n## Escalation note\n\n**From:** joseph.mathai\n**To:** sunil.bagade (Hub Manager, NSK-1), cc rukhsana.p\n**Date:** 26 Apr 2024, 11:47\n\nSunil,\n\nThree curd returns out of Nashik in eight days, tickets 118204, 118331, 118402, plus one closed as no fault found on 22 Apr that probably belongs with them. All Category A, all early routes, all \"sour\" or \"watery\" at the door.\n\nMy reading, and Rukhsana agrees: it is the season. Nashik has come out of winter fast this year and the vans are sitting in the sun at the society gates while riders do four floors on foot. Bengaluru does not get this because Bengaluru does not get 38 degrees in April. We saw something similar in Pune two summers ago and it settled once the riders started staging the crates in the stairwell instead of the van.\n\nRukhsana, please add a note to the Nashik rider briefing about crate staging and let us watch it for two weeks.\n\nSunil, nothing for you to action unless you are seeing something at the cold room end. Flag it if you are.\n\nJoseph\n\n---\n\n## Thread status\n\n**Current disposition:** Monitoring, rider briefing issued 27 Apr 2024.\n**Reviewed:** 29 Apr 2024, no further action pending.\n"
